From e814e42e7d10017c9ab0cabbefa2769e94db92b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 03:47:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: the peak that the automatic content mapping v4.0 is
 decided against can be set by hand

The automatic choices of the v4.0 setting add the 4.0 part to a video that was mastered
brighter than the TV, and they judge that against the peak that the Dolby block of the
TV's EDID declares. A TV that declares a wrong one is judged wrongly. Two settings at the
expert level: "Tone mapping v4.0: set the TV's peak by hand" (off) and the peak, 40 to 4000
cd/m2 (1000), which replaces the declared one, with a line in the log that says both. The
conversion of a luminance to the 12-bit PQ level moves to DVPeak.h, where a test runs on
the host; the one that was inline gives the same levels.

Strings: core 41120 to 41123, Estuary 32600 to 32603 (English, and Spanish for es_es, es_ar
and es_mx).
